; Preliminary (square) base: one flatten at the centre vertex.
;
; Six rays fold, not eight. The half-diagonals toward .b and .d fold 180
; degrees: each becomes a two-layer taco, one per side of the base. The
; diagonal through .a and .c stays flat (marked, so it subdivides) and spans
; both sides: the a-quarter is the front face, the c-quarter the back, the
; two tacos sit between them. All eight rays folded gives the base folded in
; half again (every face in one 45-degree wedge); the four medians alone give
; the quarter fold, which becomes this base only after a squash.
;
; Every named point lies on a crease through the centre, so the stacking
; needs points inside sectors: .q in the a-quarter, .r in the b-quarter.
; (.q over .r) puts the a-quarter on top of the b-taco, i.e. in front.

paper square

mark (through .a .c) as --ac
mark (through .b .d) as --bd
mark (map --ab onto --cd) as --h
mark (map --da onto --bc) as --v
.q = free on --ab from .a at 1/4
.r = free on --ab from .b at 1/4

flatten (--h & --bc) (--v & --cd) (--h & --da) (--v & --ab)
  (--bd & .b) (--bd & .d) (.q over .r) (toward .q)

; assert steps = 1
; assert faces = 6
